{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1131748-king-s-pennywise-is-a-beast","id":1131748,"title":"King's Pennywise is a Beast!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-20T09:32:31-07:00","id":1131748,"title":"King's Pennywise is a Beast!","content":"SPOILERS for anyone not reading the book or watching a TV series...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> First, he feeds on children's fear. We know that clown is only form for the monster inside it. It's even more apparent when you analyze his powers - he can be shapeshifter ( probably Atavism ), creating illusions that can harm victim ( Nightmares ) and regeneration ( probably Atavism ). Just see video...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-AWmzJffDRA\" data-code=\"-AWmzJffDRA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/-AWmzJffDRA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T09:55:09-07:00","id":1131758,"title":"","content":"I think to remember some writers saying they use It as inspiration when it comes to Lair and Chamber creations. Which works, since in the book It has recurring places from which it emerges, often related to previous shenanigans (the house in Neibolt Street, the abandoned factory, etc.) and having a sense of dread surrounding them. I can totally see that aspect being an idea source for Beast but, if I were to stat It in-game, I'd go with an Insatiable. Seriously, it's a fear-based shapeshifter that eats people and has a very physical Den.<br /> <br /> That said, if you give me total freedom, I'd write It as an Idigam. Shapeshifting creature born at the dawn of time? Check. Ban and banes? Check. Ability to influence both the mind and bodies of those it comes in contact with? Check. Going into hybernation after feeding or being defeated? Check. Enough power to subtly (or not so subtly) alter the environment to make it fit its whims? Check (though that can be done with Insatiable's Schism as well)<br /> <br /> I mean, there are many ways to replicate It in the CoD. Depending on the gameline you're looking at, odds are there's an Antagonist group you might work it into. Horror, Fae, Abyssal Monster... If you ask me, though, the easiest route to translate It is totally the Idigam one.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: I took the hype train straight into the face and I'm reading the book again so yeah, I gave some (read: <i>a lot</i>) thoughts about this topic","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 08-20-2017, 01:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T10:16:19-07:00","id":1131769,"title":"","content":"Sounds good! So how about Namtaru Predator with a preferance for Children, Behold my True Form and Fear is Contagious, as well as You must Obey. A refluffed Bugs Everywhere! maybe too.<br /> Atavisms are at least Relentless Hunter and Needs Must. Alien Allure would work, well, too.<br /> From the Shadows, to mimic his partial invisibility?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T22:30:19-07:00","id":1132080,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a>, looking for your thoughts later! <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a>, how would you replicate shapeshifting by Atavisms? I do not know Beast to throw powers from memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T01:49:17-07:00","id":1132123,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar38_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"38\" data-vbnamecard=\"38\">Cinder</a> absolutely right, I like that Idigam Route a lot!<br /> I was simply trying to make an IT - based beast, which is quite a fun exercise. Insatiable sounds quite good, too. Much food for thought, thanks!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> They don't. You might use a homebrew atavism or make up a nightmare to that effect, but as of core, the fear of someone being an imposter or not what why seem to be is not included. Might make a pretty kick ass Family, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T23:23:30-07:00","id":1140098,"title":"","content":"If we would do Shapeshifting Atavism for Pennywise, what would it look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T23:49:39-07:00","id":1140101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1131748-king-s-pennywise-is-a-beast?p=1140098#post1140098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we would do Shapeshifting Atavism for Pennywise, what would it look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>I made one in the 'Other Atavism Ideas?' thread called Ten Thousand Faces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T00:50:32-07:00","id":1140107,"title":"","content":"For ease of discussion, I quote <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar10397_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"10397\" data-vbnamecard=\"10397\">ajf115</a>'s homebrew Atavism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/580599-other-atavism-ideas?p=814153#post814153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Here's an idea for how this could go.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Ten Thousand Faces (Eshmaki)</u></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">No matter how horrific or vast their foe, little inspires more fear and horror in mankind than a wolf in sheep's clothing. All throughout history, in every culture, there have been tales of malicious shapeshifters, from kitsune to naga to rakshasa, no civilisation has forgotten this fear. After all, what is more terrifying than a predator who can not only take your life, wealth and livelihood but your very identity as well?</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Action:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Instant</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dice Pool:</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Normal:</span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> The Beast's flesh is quicksilver, shifting at a whim and taking on the shape and hue desired of it. The Beast is able to change superficial aspects of his appearance such as hair and skin colour, scars, tattoos, the general shape of facial features, and alter his height and girth by small amounts (not enough to alter his Size). He may also alter his apparent gender although he only alters this outwardly. A Beast who becomes female using this power will not be able to bear children, nor will a neo-male be able to sire them. This ability is not precise enough to exactly imitate another, but it does grant a number of bonus dice to disguise oneself equal to the Beast's (Lair * 2). These disguises last until the Beast wishes to dismiss them.</span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Low Satiety: </span></b><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">As the Beast's hunger grows, so too does the precision with which he can alter his own flesh. The Beast may roll Wits + Medicine to precisely imitate another whom they have seen within the last 5 days. The Beast can only imitate those parts of the body that he has seen, meaning that he will not be able to exactly imitate another unless he has seen them completely naked. In addition, the Beast may now use the basic iteration of this power to increase or decrease her Size by 1 (from her real Size), imitate missing or deformed limbs (or whole ones, if his are damaged) and create functional gender changes. In addition, the Beast may create non-functional supernatural features, provided that these do not grossly alter the shape of his body. For example, a Beast could create a non-functional third eye, but not a pair of wings. These changes will persist even after the Beast has gained enough Satiety to become Sated or more but changes which are only possible with this level of Satiety can only be undone while in Low Satiety. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Satiety Expenditure:</b> </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With the expenditure of a dot of Satiety, the Beast can not only change her own flesh but also that of others. These changes are </span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>not</u></span><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> permanent, but last a number of weeks equal to the Beast's Lair. The Beast can only make changes in others that he could in himself with his level of Satiety (before spending the dot). Unwilling participants can resist with Stamina + Supernatural Advantage vs the Beast's Wits + Lair. Some Beasts use this ability to give others a new life, away from the fear of pursuers or old enemies. Others pose as exceptionally talented plastic surgeons or backstreet doctors. More malicious Beasts force others into lives that they do not want or even steal their lives altogether, taking their shapes and giving them new ones, shapes which have no life at all.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>So if we assume Pennywise as Beast, the clown is once human host to the IT Horror in it. But from reading of Ten Thousand Faces, it would be hard to replicate all the fantastic visions the Pennywise is showing to Losers Club. Also, Pennywise sounds more as Anakim to me than Eshmaki - he does not sounds as really 'rising fear by being next to you' - recall me, Anakim can learn Eshmaki's Atavism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-14-2017, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}